{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender render passes blender render passes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","fileName":"Blender Render Passes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Render Passes","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-07 23:25\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Blender Video Editing and Compositing]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Video Editing and Compositing","Multi-Pass Render Compositing","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender render passes blender render passes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","fileName":"Blender Render Passes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Render Passes","heading":"Blender Render Passes","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A view layer selects which scene collections participate in a render, while passes separate components of that layer. A pass may isolate depth, shadows, normals, object indices, or another kind of image data for later adjustment.\n\nRendering a static environment separately from a moving character can avoid repeating expensive work. Z-depth and other passes then help the Compositor make elements fit together even when they were not rendered in one combined scene.\n\nGress's visual-effects examples extend this principle to independent color, diffuse, specular, light, shadow, normal, luminosity, and depth contributions. The Compositor can merge those passes after rendering, but a property baked into a lighting pass cannot be adjusted as freely as one given its own pass. See [[Multi-Pass Render Compositing]].","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Video Editing and Compositing","Multi-Pass Render Compositing","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"blender render passes blender render passes","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Blender Render Passes.md","fileName":"Blender Render Passes.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Blender Render Passes","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf]]\n[[digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Blender Video Editing and Compositing","Multi-Pass Render Compositing","blenderfordummies4thedition.pdf","digitalvisualeffectsandcompositing.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}